---

---

This is the **single source of truth** blueprint you can paste into Notion and follow from Day-0 → Global scale.

It contains the architecture, agents & supervisors, event choreography, storage map, security & compliance controls, observability, dev & infra scaffolding, roadmaps, milestones, KPIs and runbooks. Use it as the canonical reference for product, eng, infra, and ops.

---

# 1 — Executive summary (one-liner)

F3Next is an event-driven, multi-agent system that **automates ERP selection, configuration, data import, testing, and ongoing support** for manufacturers — built with Temporal supervisors, Kafka event fabric, LangChain agents, Postgres + S3 canonical store, vector DB memory, and enterprise-grade observability & security.

---

# 2 — Goals & success criteria

- **MVP goal:** automate intake → ERP recommendation → template generation → validated dry-run import → staging test → human-approved production import → handover + support planner.
- **Production goals:** multi-region, per-customer secure instances, auditable writes, <98% dry-run pass automation, mapping automation ≥70% with confidence ≥0.8, safe cost & token budgets.
- **Business KPIs:** time-to-first-dryrun ≤48h, import success rate ≥95%, average mapping human interventions per project ≤20%.

---

# 3 — High-level architecture (diagram summary)

- Event bus: **Kafka** (topics partitioned by `project_id`)
- Orchestration: **Temporal** (supervisors as durable workflows)
- Agents: containerized microservices (K8s + Ray for heavy tasks)
- Storage: **Postgres** (canonical state), **S3** (blobs), **Vector DB** (Pinecone/Qdrant), **Redis** (session cache)
- Secrets: **Vault**; Monitoring: **Prometheus**, **Grafana**, **Jaeger**, **LangSmith** (LLM traces)
- Infra provisioning: **Terraform + Terraform Cloud** or API-driven IaC, per-customer workspaces

---

# 4 — Complete agent inventory (roles) — canonical list

## Supervisors (Temporal workflows)

- Implementation Supervisor (project-level)
- Selection Supervisor
- Discovery Supervisor
- Ingest Supervisor
- Config Supervisor
- QA Supervisor
- Support Supervisor
- Infra Supervisor

## Worker / Functional Agents

- Intake Agent
- Discovery Agent (ERP recommendation)
- Pricing Agent
- Payment Agent
- Configuration Agent (deep discovery)
- Template Agent
- Data Validation Agent
- Mapping Agent
- Retriever Agent (vector fetcher)
- Generator Agent (prompt composer / LLM calls)
- ETL / Import Agent (dry-run + prod chunked import)
- Rollback Agent
- Config Agent (apply ERP configs)
- Testing Agent (staging + prod tests)
- Training Agent (generate training materials)
- Support Planner Agent (task planning)
- Support Agent (RAG-powered helpdesk)
- Knowledge Agent (KB updates & retraining triggers)
- Infra Provisioning Agent
- Monitor Agent (observability exporter)
- Security Agent (secrets & policy checks)

